{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make one with the subject’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeSubscription()"},{"type":"text","text":". It subscribes when it is made, exactly like the subject’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CurrentValueSubject"},{"type":"text","text":"’s subscription starts with the current value, and every value sent after that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is buffered for it, without limit, until "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},{"type":"text","text":" returns it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The difference is cancellation. Cancelling a task waiting in an iterator’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"text":" ends that iterator’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subscription and discards its buffer. Cancelling a task waiting in a subscription’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},{"text":" throws","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"text":" from that call only: the subscription stays subscribed, and a later ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},{"text":" returns the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values sent before and after the cancellation, in order. That suits a consumer that runs in rounds, such as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch run that is cancelled and started again, and must not miss what was sent between rounds.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The subscription unsubscribes when its last copy is released. It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncIteratorProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":", so an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operator can read it through "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncIteratorSequence"},{"type":"text","text":"; a cancelled read then ends that operator’s run with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"type":"text","text":" and leaves the subscription for the next run."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Example","type":"heading","anchor":"Example"},{"code":["let events = PassthroughSubject<String>()","let subscription = events.makeSubscription()","","let firstRound = Task { try await subscription.next() }","firstRound.cancel() \/\/ Throws CancellationError from that wait; nothing is lost.","_ = await firstRound.result","","events.send(\"launch\")","events.send(\"login\")","let first = try await subscription.next()  \/\/ \"launch\"","let second = try await subscription.next() \/\/ \"login\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wait on a subscription from one task at a time. Calling ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" while another call on the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subscription is still waiting traps.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}],"externalID":"s:7Afluent19SubjectSubscriptionV","title":"SubjectSubscription","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubjectSubscription.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription.swift#L40"},"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubjectSubscription"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A place in a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that a consumer can stop waiting on and come back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to, keeping every value sent in between."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/AsyncIteratorProtocol-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/ScI"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","abstract":[],"title":"Afluent","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent","type":"topic"},"doc://Afluent/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype"},"doc://Afluent/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/SubjectSubscription":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription","title":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A place in a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" that a consumer can stop waiting on and come back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to, keeping every value sent in between."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/CurrentValueSubject":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A subject that broadcasts its current value and all subsequent values to multiple consumers.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It can also handle completion events, including normal termination and failure with an error.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This 